    "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the cost of one plastic chair and one portable table, and then calculate how much Manny will have left after purchasing one portable table and two chairs.\n\nStep 1: Determine the cost of one plastic chair.\nWe know that five plastic chairs cost $55. Therefore, the cost of one plastic chair is:\n\\[\n\\text{Cost of one plastic chair} = \\frac{55}{5} = 11 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Determine the cost of one portable table.\nWe know that three plastic chairs cost as much as one portable table. Therefore, the cost of one portable table is:\n\\[\n\\text{Cost of one portable table} = 3 \\times 11 = 33 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Calculate the total cost of one portable table and two chairs.\nThe total cost of one portable table and two chairs is:\n\\[\n\\text{Total cost} = 33 + 2 \\times 11 = 33 + 22 = 55 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Determine how much Manny will have left after the purchase.\nManny has $100. After spending $55, the amount of money he will have left is:\n\\[\n\\text{Money left} = 100 - 55 = 45 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{45}\n\\]",
